From: KV Rosetta <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] server: advertise slot checkpoint persistence and report coverage

Local KV Rosetta integration patch, applied on top of upstream PR #26004.
Kept separate so upstream provenance stays auditable.

Adds a machine-readable runtime protocol so a client never has to infer
checkpoint support from an architecture name, a commit, a filename, a
strings(1) match, or an artifact size - all of which describe the build
rather than the behaviour.

  /props           slot_checkpoint_persistence, slot_checkpoint_format,
                   sequence_state_version, per-blob support flags,
                   active_checkpoint_state_classes, and the live target
                   context's K/V cache types
  save/restore     n_checkpoints, checkpoint_bytes, and the newest
                   checkpoint's n_tokens, pos_min and pos_max

--- a/tools/server/server-task.h
+++ b/tools/server/server-task.h
@@ -526,6 +526,14 @@
     size_t n_bytes;
     double t_ms;
 
+    // KV Rosetta: checkpoint metadata, so a client can verify what it actually got
+    // instead of inferring it from the file size or from the architecture name.
+    size_t    n_checkpoints    = 0;
+    size_t    checkpoint_bytes = 0;
+    int64_t   ckpt_n_tokens    = 0;
+    llama_pos ckpt_pos_min     = -1;
+    llama_pos ckpt_pos_max     = -1;
+
     virtual json to_json() override;
 };
 
